Changes from 2.4.1, made by SOAJS:
- only the password and refresh_token grants and authorise() are kept; the authorization code,
  client credentials and extended grants, errorHandler and lockdown are not;
- grant() takes the user lookup per request (req.oauth2GetUser), so a shared model is never
  changed between requests;
- the refresh_token grant consumes the used refresh token (model.consumeRefreshToken) before
  issuing new ones, answers "Invalid refresh token" when nothing was consumed (another request used
  it first), and puts it back (model.restoreRefreshToken) when the new tokens cannot be saved;
- the Basic authorization header is parsed here (basic-auth 0.0.1 rules), without the package.
- a token's expires must be a valid Date: null, a string, a missing value or an invalid Date has
  expired (2.4.1 let null, a string and an invalid Date never expire).
